# Project quality (SSOT)

## OpenSpec

- OpenSpec is the source of truth for change requirements.
- Read related specs/design/tasks before coding.
- Do not invent business rules silently; escalate ambiguity.
- Update the spec when requirements or decisions change.
- Do not edit unrelated archived OpenSpec changes.

## Quality

- New business logic ships with tests.
- Bug fixes preferably include a regression test.
- Do not disable checks to force a green result.
- Do not claim a check passed if it was not run.
- Prefer clear, maintainable code.
- Comment business rules, non-obvious decisions, limits, and trade-offs — not every line.

## Data and analytics

- Store raw Trello history; compute metrics from stored events and workflow rules.
- Never invent missing events or timestamps.
- Incomplete history → document and warn; do not silently fill gaps.
- Timestamps in UTC in storage; timezone for display and period boundaries.

## Security and Git

- Secrets only in env / protected config; never commit real secrets.
- No tokens/passwords in logs or API responses to the client.
- Trello calls only from backend.
- No automatic commit, push, or deploy.
